//|                                                                  |
//|  v12 CHANGELOG — surgical, everything from v11 preserved:        |
//|                                                                  |
//|   1. ENTRY BREATHING ROOM. Initial stop sits at                  |
//|      (T_SlNoiseBuf + T_SlEntryBuf) x ATR beyond the signal line  |
//|      — wider at the moment of entry so an ordinary noise-dip     |
//|      doesn't clip a correct trade. Ratchets back to normal over  |
//|      6 bars OR the instant profitR ≥ 0.8, whichever comes first. |
//|      Position size shrinks proportionally in LotFor: cash risk   |
//|      is UNCHANGED. Not looser risk — smarter placement.          |
//|                                                                  |
//|   2. CONFLUENCE TIER SIZING. Base 0.01. When M1/M3/M5 + M15 all  |
//|      agree with the direction of the flip, size is 0.03. When    |
//|      H1 + H4 also agree (the full stack), 0.05 — but 0.05 is     |
//|      gated behind proven expectancy (≥0.30R over 30 TREND trades)|
//|      so it unlocks once the record earns it. Rare by design:     |
//|      daily cap 8. Every non-confluent trade stays at base size.  |
//|                                                                  |
//|   3. FAST-SCRATCH FILTER. A tight, quick stop-out (<0.5R held    |
//|      under ~5 bars) no longer counts toward the consecutive-loss |
//|      streak. This was the "6 losses in a row" pause you flagged: |
//|      4 signal-line scratches at trend starts is NORMAL on this   |
//|      system, not evidence anything's wrong. Only meaningful      |
//|      losses accumulate. InpMaxConsecLoss also raised 4 → 8.      |
//|                                                                  |
//|   4. APEX ON BY DEFAULT. A good 15m ride is exactly the trade    |
//|      that makes the day. House-bias already prevents it fighting |
//|      the fast timeframes.                                        |
//|                                                                  |
//|   5. GUARDIAN H1 EXIT SOFTENED. H1 alone against a fresh M1/M3   |
//|      trade is not evidence to close — H1 hasn't caught up yet.   |
//|      Now requires H1 against AND (M15 also against OR real loss).|
//|      Was closing valid fast-timeframe scalps prematurely.        |
//|                                                                  |
//|   6. AUTOPSY AUTO-TIGHTEN ENABLED. The EA now genuinely learns   |
//|      from real loss patterns — the fast-scratch filter keeps     |
//|      noise out of the sample so it only tightens on real signal. |
//|                                                                  |
//|   7. PINE v15 ALERT FORMAT. ReadPineSignals now parses the       |
//|      optional TAG (NORMAL|REENTRY) and TIER (0|2|3) fields sent  |
//|      by APEX 15. Backward compatible with the old 6-field format.|
